Copied host buffers (copied.rs) read and write only pages the program still maps. A copy whose pages no buffer lies in any
longer (its keys gone, Copied::unname) is neither copied in nor merged back, nor is one whose pages the process no longer maps,
asked of the kernel at each copy in and merge back (mapped_writable / mapped_readable, mach_vm_region on macOS): WindowServer
frees a no-copy buffer's memory, or a part of it past a region's end, while the buffer lives, which Metal's GPU never reads where
no command reads it; an unnamed reach (CopiesReached::all) compared every copy, and its commits crashed in
copy_in_untagged/copy_in_blocks at login.

